cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "UbboTELORNA"
abstract: >
  UbboTELORNA annotates ancient, conserved genomic elements — telomeres,
  subtelomeric tandem repeats, rRNA genes, tRNA genes, and centromere
  candidates — in genome assemblies, with built-in low-complexity masking
  and optional evolutionary/score-distribution analysis of the resulting
  annotations. Named after Ubbo-Sathla, the primordial source of all
  terrestrial life in the Lovecraft–Smith Mythos.
authors:
